.TH ICON 2
.SH NAME
icon \- the interface's glyphs, at any size in any colour
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "draw.m";
include "tk.m";
include "icon.m";
icon := load Icon Icon->PATH;

init:    fn(d: ref Draw->Display): string;
mask:    fn(name: string, size: int): (ref Draw->Image, string);
paint:   fn(name: string, size, colour: int):
             (ref Draw->Image, ref Draw->Image, string);
tkimage: fn(t: ref Tk->Toplevel, tkname, name: string,
             size, colour: int): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Icon
draws the glyphs of InferNode's interface: folders and files, mounts and
devices, the arrows and operations of a window.
Each is an SVG file,
.BI /icons/ui/ name .svg ,
drawn by
.B readsvg
(see
.IR imagefile (2))
at the size asked for, so a glyph is sharp at any size and on a display of
any scale, and painted in a colour the caller gives, as a rule one of the
current theme's (see
.IR lucitheme (2)),
so a theme switch is a repaint.
.PP
.B Init
takes the display the images are to be made on, a
.BR Toplevel 's
for a Tk program.
.B Mask
returns the glyph
.I name
drawn at
.I size
by
.I size
pixels as a
.B GREY8
image: 255 where the glyph is, 0 where it is not, to draw a colour
through.
A glyph drawn once at a size is kept, and asking for it again draws
nothing.
.B Paint
returns an image of
.I colour
(an
.B RGBA32
value, as
.B Display.color
takes) and the glyph's mask, to draw with
.BR Image.draw .
.B Tkimage
makes the Tk image
.I tkname
in
.I t
the glyph painted in
.IR colour :
it creates the image if there is none of that name, and replaces it,
repainting it wherever it is shown, if there is.
The image is created even if the glyph cannot be drawn, so widgets
naming it are still made, blank.
.PP
Each returns a diagnostic string on error: a name with a
.B /
in it, or that is no glyph, a size outside 1 to 1024, or a draw device
that cannot be had.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/ui/*.svg
The glyphs, from Tabler Icons (MIT licence,
.BR /icons/ui/LICENSE ).
.TP
.B /icons/ui/LIST
Their names.
To add one, add its name and run
.BR tools/update-icons.sh ,
which fetches every glyph listed from the pinned Tabler release.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/icon.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw-image (2),
.IR imagefile (2),
.IR tk (2)
